<article class="env-lemma" id="095Z">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/095Z">Lemma <span data-tag="095Z">59.76.4</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a quasi-compact and quasi-separated scheme. Let $\Lambda $ be a Noetherian ring. Let $K \in D(X_{\acute{e}tale}, \Lambda )$ and $b \in \mathbf{Z}$ such that $H^ b(K)$ is constructible. Then there exist a sheaf $\mathcal{F}$ which is a finite direct sum of $j_{U!}\underline{\Lambda }$ with $U \in \mathop{\mathrm{Ob}}\nolimits (X_{\acute{e}tale})$ affine and a map $\mathcal{F}[-b] \to K$ in $D(X_{\acute{e}tale}, \Lambda )$ inducing a surjection $\mathcal{F} \to H^ b(K)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Represent $K$ by a complex $\mathcal{K}^\bullet $ of sheaves of $\Lambda $-modules. Consider the surjection 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{\mathrm{Ker}}(\mathcal{K}^ b \to \mathcal{K}^{b + 1}) \longrightarrow H^ b(K)  \]
</div>
    <p>
       By Modules on Sites, Lemma <a href="/tag/093B" data-tag="093B">18.30.6</a> we may choose a surjection $\bigoplus _{i \in I} j_{U_ i!} \underline{\Lambda } \to \mathop{\mathrm{Ker}}(\mathcal{K}^ b \to \mathcal{K}^{b + 1})$ with $U_ i$ affine. For $I' \subset I$ finite, denote $\mathcal{H}_{I'} \subset H^ b(K)$ the image of $\bigoplus _{i \in I'} j_{U_ i!} \underline{\Lambda }$. By Lemma <a href="/tag/095P" data-tag="095P">59.71.8</a> we see that $\mathcal{H}_{I'} = H^ b(K)$ for some $I' \subset I$ finite. The lemma follows taking $\mathcal{F} = \bigoplus _{i \in I'} j_{U_ i!} \underline{\Lambda }$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>